The angle of depression of the base of the tree from the top of the building is $58^\circ$.

If the base of the tree is 13 m from the building, what is the height of the building, correct to one decimal place?

\exfigure{710_q4_1}

solutions.latex:
The angle of elevation of the top of the building from the base of the tree is also $58^\circ$ (alternate angles).

\exfigure{710_q4_s1}

$\tan 58^\circ = \dfrac{h}{13}$, so $h = 13\tan 58^\circ = 20.8$ m.
